{
 "$schema_note": "Anchor records for the marketplace trust layer. Each record: a Nostr event (kind 8555, signed by the marketplace-anchor pubkey below) carrying sha256 digests of the live agent surfaces at fetch time (/directory.json, /live/snapshot.json, /live/models.json, /live/uptime.json), published to public relays, its canonical serialization stored as <event_id>.evt (sha256(.evt) == event_id per NIP-01) and stamped into Bitcoin via OpenTimestamps (<event_id>.evt.ots). The `ots` field is re-derived from the .ots file on every run: \"bitcoin\" once a Bitcoin block-header attestation is present (block heights in ots_bitcoin_blocks), \"pending\" while only calendar attestations are \u2014 a fresh stamp takes hours to confirm, so the newest record reading \"pending\" is normal. how_to_check: (1) sha256 the .evt file and confirm it equals the event id; (2) verify the event signature against anchor_pubkey (NIP-01 schnorr); (3) `ots info <event_id>.evt.ots` lists the Bitcoin block heights with NO node required \u2014 check any of them on a block explorer by hand; for a fully trust-minimised check run `ots verify -d <event_id> <event_id>.evt.ots` against your own Bitcoin node (it speaks to a node over RPC, not to an explorer); (4) fetch the event by id from the listed relays for the third-party copy. The repo history of this folder is itself an additional weak anchor.",
